    text+=['','Available support shrinks with horizon because recorded futures are short and executions terminate. `release_metrics.json:same_3s_cohort` also holds a common30-root horizon comparison; neither cohort supports a strong general3-second claim. Increasing error with horizon is expected. Undercoverage and unrealistically persistent intentions are the problem, not failure to decrease absolute error.','',
           '| Full minus baseline ES |0.5s paired CI|1s paired CI|2s paired CI|3s paired CI|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
    for name,values in s['forecast_paired_deltas'].items():text.append('|'+name+'|'+'|'.join(ci(values[str(h)]) for h in (.5,1,2,3))+'|')
    text+=['','Learning improves over structured kinematics at0.5/1seconds, while2/3-second superiority is inconclusive. The full association mixture does not establish superiority over the learned-graph ablation. Memory CV is weaker here on visible-target scores; this does not prove that memory is unnecessary for temporarily hidden people. A comprehensive hidden-recall/false-track score remains absent.','',
           f"One native-step development scores are {a['one_native_step']['learned']['mean']:.5f} learned versus {a['one_native_step']['memory_cv']['mean']:.5f} memory CV over203roots. This is a descriptive teacher-conditioned legal-root transition test, not demonstrated heldout superiority. Mean mode entropy is {a['mode_diagnostics']['mean_entropy_nats']:.3f}nats, minimum mode probability averaged across slots is {a['mode_diagnostics']['mean_minimum_mode_probability']:.3f}, and target-pair separation is {a['mode_diagnostics']['mean_target_pair_separation_mps']:.3f}m/s. These establish distinct parameter components, not calibrated behavioral multimodality.", '',
           '## Same-target observation conditioning','',
           'Both arms use the same target at root+2s, the same actual executed prefix and projected survival evidence. The posterior additionally receives the tenth arrived legal action observation (about0.48s). No root future is injected into its state. Positive means an informative originally-visible target is detected; reappearance is a source-tracker proxy. The predeclared non-inferiority margin is+0.020m, with one-sided95% upper bound; fewer than100roots or30scenes is inconclusive for broad claims.','',
           '| Category |Roots / scenes|Posterior−prior ES, 95% CI|Upper one-sided95%|Decision|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|']
    for name,v in s['conditioning'].items():text.append(f"|{name}|{v['roots']} / {v['scenes']}|{ci(v)}|{v.get('one_sided_upper95',float('nan')):.3f}|{v['decision']}|")
    text+=['','The overall and informative-positive point estimates worsen on holdout, unlike development. Non-inferiority is not established. CIs and small support do not justify asserting universal observation harm either. Reappearance, aged tracks and dense cases are adverse but weakly supported. Missing/occluded observations make no update and produce identical scores by construction; their flat line is not evidence of successful negative-evidence inference. Real certified-empty performance is unavailable.','',
           'Failure investigation identifies timestamp-controlled comparison, count/association fragmentation, overly narrow motion innovations and a mismatch between the real and coarse observation laws. The positional process-noise revision helped development slightly but did not resolve holdout conditioning. No further parameters were tuned on holdout. The next experiment must separate association error from dynamics using ancestry-preserving scoring and an explicitly offline oracle-association diagnostic.','',
           '## Native events and candidate decisions','',
           'Binary event probabilities are scored at their legally planned/evaluated horizon. Early contact establishes the positive event; it does not shorten the probability horizon used for calibration. Administrative noncontact censoring is excluded; this heldout run had none. Native events use recorded articulated contact and geodesic/fallback PSC labels. The appearance event is a previously-untracked identity proxy, not calibrated native endpoint visibility.','',
           '| Event |Brier, 95% CI|CV / constant baseline Brier|Predicted|Observed|Probability bias, 95% CI|Within-root concordance|','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
